---
layout: base.njk
title: Field Reports & Notes | Mukundara Hills Tiger Reserve
description: Field reports and field notes from the Mukundara landscape and wider Rajasthan ecology, with author credit, bilingual reading where available, and no sensitive wildlife locations.
activeSection: field-reports
---

<section class="page-hero" aria-label="Field reports introduction">
  <p class="eyebrow">Field Reports</p>
  <h1>Field reports and notes from Rajasthan’s living landscapes.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Field reports bring local observation, ecological context, and careful documentation together.
    This section will grow into a readable archive of notes, articles, field evidence, and translated material.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-label="Field reports list">
  <div class="report-list">
    {% for report in fieldReports %}
      <article class="report-card">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">{{ report.topic }}</p>
          <h2><a href="{{ report.href }}">{{ report.title }}</a></h2>
          <p class="hindi-title" lang="hi">{{ report.hindiTitle }}</p>
          <p>{{ report.summary }}</p>
        </div>
        <footer class="report-meta">
          <span>By {{ report.author }}</span>
          <span>{{ report.date }}</span>
        </footer>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section narrow" aria-label="Contribution note">
  <h2>Contribution standard</h2>
  <p>
    Reports should preserve author credit, avoid sensitive coordinates, and separate direct observation from
    interpretation. Photo and video evidence can be added once captions, dates, and permissions are confirmed.
  </p>
</section>
